\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Gold $1,247.30; Often Rises In September - BarCap\b0\par\par\uc2 1,750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2010\par 01:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 2321 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold early in Sydney $1,247.30/oz, down 50 cents this morning, a tidy overnight gain from intraday low of $1,232 attributed to safe haven buying. \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  says September often a bullish month for gold with price rising in 21 of past 30 years. More recently, during current "great" bull run, gold up 9 in 11 years, with September often when price rallied out of long-standing ranges, signaling resumption of secular trend, it says. Technically, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says that after close above previous $1,242/$1,245 barrier, "we are inclined to expect further near-term gains for gold in September, given the strong seasonal bias associated with the month during the past 13 years." While nothing guaranteed, strong close overnight suggests further gains "very likely." Consolidation this week above $1,229 bullish with high at $1,265 the primary target ahead of $1,280, then $1,300.(ray.brindal@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2319 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei likely to trade narrowly between 8750-8900 vs 8824.06 yesterday close(down 3.6%). While distinct possibility index could test year-low of 8807.41, analysts say further selling likely to be limited by better-than-expected U.S. consumer confidence and housing data, and buying by Japanese pension funds. "The Nikkei may test below 8800 (if USD/JPY falls below 84), but expectations for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely provide support at that level," says Kazuhiro Takahashi, general manager at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets. Real estate shares likely to outperform market following positive housing starts data in Japan and BOJ's easing measures, while chipmakers such as \uc2 Tokyo Electron\uc2  (8035.TO) expected to continue falling on overnight decline in Intel (INTC) shares. Nikkei 225 September futures ended Chicago trading at 8830 vs Osaka close at 8800.(kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2315 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may drop to 83.70 as investor sentiment remains risk-averse after FOMC minutes overnight highlighted slowdown of U.S. economic recovery, ways Fed can bolster growth, says Minoru Shioiri, senior dealer at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities. Says EUR/JPY may fall in tandem to 106.00. Markets focusing on U.S. ISM manufacturing PMI for August due 1400 GMT -- reading likely 52.5 vs 55.5 in July, shows Dow Jones poll of economists -- if worse than expected, market sentiment would shift further toward risk-off, sending investors into safe-heaven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as JPY. EUR/USD may trade in 1.2620-1.2720 range vs last 1.2688. USD/JPY may trade in 83.70-84.60 band vs last 84.15. EUR/JPY may trade in 106.00-107.20 range vs last 106.63.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2310 GMT [Dow Jones] BIS's triennial \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey shows USD/JPY's average daily turnover rises to $568 billion in April 2010; that compares with $328 billion in April 2004, year when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Nearly-doubled market volumes suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF may find it very difficult stopping JPY's rise via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . What's more, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF official recently told Dow Jones that if it steps into market, amount of JPY-selling would be much less than in past campaigns. BIS survey shows activity by 