esday, most active ASX milling wheat deliverable January in NSW eased A$1.50 to A$291.00/metric ton; ASX milling wheat deliverable January in WA down A$3.30 at A$309.50. (ray.brindal@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2239 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD tipping higher early, largely on 'buy on rumor, sell on news' ahead of Aussie 2Q GDP at 0130 GMT, though strategists at NAB warn move may not last. "Any boost to the AUD from this morning's Australian GDP report for 2Q could prove short-lived unless economic reports improve sentiment towards the global economic outlook in the major economies," says NAB \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist John Kyriakopoulos, noting today's China PMI data is key. AUD/USD recently at 0.8932, up from early morning trade around 0.8902, with NAB tipping support at 0.8860 and then 0.8815. NAB says resistance is at 0.8980 to 0.9000. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com) [ 08-31-10 1921ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100831e68v000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
