\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 31\b0\par\par\uc2 2,694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2010\par 09:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA APRIL-JUNE GDP UP 8.8% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian economy grew 8.8% from a year earlier in the April-June quarter, driven mainly by the strong performance of the manufacturing sector and services such as trade, hotels and communications, according to data issued by the Central Statistical Organisation Tuesday. (publishd 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION EDGES UP, MAY STALL AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's industrial production edged up in July due to higher output in the general machinery and chemicals sectors, but the slight rise is unlikely to dispel concerns that gains could stall in the months ahead as the country's economy slows. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER DEFENDS BOJ STEP; THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister defended the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday from criticism that its latest policy step was too modest to halt the yen's rise, suggesting the minister may refrain from demanding more monetary easing for some time. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT NARROWEST SINCE 1989 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia posted its narrowest current account deficit in more than 20 years in the second quarter as a once-in-a-century mining boom continues to reshape the economy, putting it on the path of virtually unrivalled prosperity among developed economies even as the global backdrop remains murky. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT BEATS FORECASTS; OUTLOOK CLOUDY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stronger than expected growth in South Korea's July industrial production showed yet again that the recovery remains solid despite increased external uncertainties, but the data also suggest the country won't be free from the slower growth momentum in the U.S. and China for much longer. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA PBOC, HK'S MING PAO DENY BOND-LOSS RUMORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denied rumors that the bank's chief had fled after posting big bond losses, while a Hong Kong newspaper denied being the source of the rumors. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: NZ FINANCE FIRM SOUTH CANTERBURY FINANCE COLLAPSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Canterbury Finance Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . collapsed Tuesday owing just under NZ$2 billion, being the latest in a string of financing companies that have cracked under the pressure of heavy debt burdens, liquidity issues and the burst in the New Zealand property bubble. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ JULY DWELLING CONSENT DATA SUGGEST MARKET WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of residential building permits excluding apartments fell, suggesting the property market is anemic and leading economists to further question whether the economy is sufficiently robust for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to again raise the official cash rate. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA IMPOSES ANTISUBSIDY TARIFF ON CHICKEN PRODUCTS FROM U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has imposed an antisubsidy tariff of 4.0% to 30.3% on chicken products imported from the U.S. from Monday, the Ministry of Commerce said in a statement following a final ruling on the tariff level. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: TO DROP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -SWAP ARRANGEMENTS FROM G-20 AGENDA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea won't pursue escalating existing regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -swap arrangements to a global level as part of global financial safety nets--an idea it had wanted to take concrete shape at the Group of 20 leading economies summit in November. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA MAY RAISE IDR3 TLN-IDR6 TLN VIA SAMURAI BOND ISSUE -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia may raise between IDR3 trillion and IDR6 trillion through Samurai bond issuance expected later this year, Finance Minister Agus Martowardoyo said Tuesday. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENHE COMMERCIAL HOLDINGS SEEKS TO PAY AROUND 13% ON 5.5-YEAR DOLLAR BOND -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Renhe Commercial Holdings Co. is seeking to pay a yield of around 13% on a proposed 5.5-year U.S. dollar bond, a person familiar with the offering said Tuesday. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: CLEARING THE AIR WITH A NEW AUSSIE POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Things have become very messy in Australian politics. The best way to clear the air might be another election. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHARTING ASIA: AUSSIE MAY RISE TO US$0.9082, US$0.9221 N/T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar jumped 0.37 percent against the U.S. dollar Tuesday on upbeat Australian data, and looks set to advance further in coming days. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: NZ FINANCE FIRM SOUTH CANTERBURY FINANCE COLLAPSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Canterbury Finance Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . collapsed Tuesday owing just under NZ$2 billion, being the latest in a string of financing companies that have cracked under the pressure of heavy debt burdens, liquidity issues and the burst in the New Zealand property bubble. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ETIC: TO INVEST Y350B IN JAPAN AIRLINES INTERNATIONAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Enterprise Initiative Turnaround Corporation said Tuesday it will invest Y350 billion in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan Airlines International Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to make it a wholly owned unit. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO INVEST $70M TO BOOST APPLIANCE PRODUCTION IN POLAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday said it will invest $70 million by 2015 to expand its appliance production facilities in Wroclaw, Poland to lower costs and increase its market presence in Europe. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TOSHIBA STARTS MASS PRODUCING HIGHER-DENSITY NAND CHIPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has started mass producing higher-density NAND flash memory chips, allowing it to boost capacity and cut costs amid fierce competition with its main rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HYUNDAI HOME SHOPPING: IPO TO RAISE KRW270 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Home Shopping Network Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it will raise KRW270 billion via an initial public offering in South Korea after pricing the share offer at the top of the indicative range. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RUSAL SWINGS TO 1ST-HALF NET PROFIT US$1.27 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Co. Rusal\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLC, the world's biggest aluminum producer by output, reported Tuesday it swung to a first-half net profit because of higher aluminum prices and said it plans to launch depositary receipts in Russia before the end of this year. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =GM DAEWOO TO LAUNCH ALPHEON SEDAN TO BOOST LOCAL SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GM Daewoo Auto & Technology Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the South Korean unit of Detroit-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Tuesday it will add the Alpheon sub-large size sedan to its product lineup next Tuesday to help boost sales in the domestic market. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: POSCO CONSIDERING EQUITY INVESTMENT IN NORWAY'S ELKEM - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Posco is considering a potential equity investment in Norway's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Elkem AS\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday, as the world's fourth-largest steelmaker by revenue pushes to diversify its business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ensure future growth. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: CENTRO FY LOSS A$652.7M; IN RESTRUCTURE TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beleaguered shopping malls owner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Centro Properties Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday signaled its recovery is far from complete, reporting a A$652.7 million annual loss and acknowledging its debt load remains unsustainable. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAILAND'S 3 MAJOR TELCOS ENTER 3G LICENSE AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's three major telecommunication companies have, via their units, been given initial approval to take part in the auction for licenses for third generation services, the National Telecommunication Commission, or NTC, said Tuesday. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: TAIWAN REJECTS AIG SALE OF TAIWAN UNIT TO CHINA STRATEGIC-LED GROUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan government rejected a bid by \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Strategic Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Primus Financial Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for \f28 \uc2 \f2 American International Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Taiwanese life insurance unit Tuesday, Hwang Jung-chiou, vice minister of the Ministry of Economic Affairs, said Tuesday. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAIICHI SANKYO UPS 1H GROUP NET PROFIT VIEW TO Y33.00B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daiichi Sankyo Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday revised upward its earnings outlook for the first half ending Sept. 30, supported by strong U.S. sales and a delay in booking some expenses to the second half. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BUMI RESOURCES AIMS TO PARE DOWN DEBT; 1H NET DOWN 30% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Bumi Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that it aims to reduce its debt level significantly to improve its full-year earnings after reporting a 30% drop in first-half net profit. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIR NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  INCREASING WEEKLY CAPACITY BY 9,500 SEATS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to increase its weekly capacity on domestic routes by 9,500 seats from early February as the recovery in the tourism industry is gaining traction. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QUANTA COMPUTER 2ND-QUARTER NET PROFIT UP 4% AT NT$5.1 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Quanta Computer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its second-quarter net profit rose 4% from a year earlier, helped by a recovery in consumer demand for electronic products. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GALAXY ENTERTAINMENT 1ST-HALF UNDERLYING NET SOARS TO HK$608 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Galaxy Entertainment Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its first-half underlying net profit rose sharply from a year earlier because of a big jump in casino gambling revenue in Macau. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JINDAL STEEL & POWER\f28 \uc2 \f2  BIDS FOR 60% STAKE IN ZIMBABWE STEEL COMPANY - EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jindal Steel & Power Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has submitted a fresh bid to acquire a 60% stake in state-run Zimbabwe Iron & Steel Co. Ltd., a company executive said Tuesday. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHUN TAK 1ST-HALF UNDERLYING NET NEARLY DOUBLES TO HK$61 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-08-10 0709GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Conglomerate Shun Tak Holdings Ltd., run by Pansy Ho, the daughter of Macau casino tycoon Stanley Ho, said Tuesday its first-half underlying net profit nearly doubled from a year earlier due to a reenergized property market. (published 0611 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GUANGZHOU AUTOMOBILE 1ST-HALF NET PROFIT SURGES TO CNY2.31 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese auto maker Guangzhou Automobile Group Co. said Tuesday its first-half net profit almost quadrupled from a year earlier, because Beijing's stimulus measures boosted vehicle sales. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PROMOS TECHNOLOGIES 1ST-HALF NET LOSS NARROWS TO NT$4.01 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Memory-chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 ProMOS Technologies Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported Tuesday its first-half net loss narrowed to NT$4.01 billion from NT$11.14 billion a year earlier. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTHERN CROSS MEDIA FY NET LOSS A$82.7M AS US DIVESTMENT WEIGHS ON RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Southern Cross Media Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday reported an A$82.7 million net loss after it booked a A$102.6 loss from its divested regional U.S. newspaper \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAILAND'S 3 MAJOR TELECOM FIRMS ENTER 3G LICENSE AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's three major telecommunication companies have, via their units, been given initial approval to take part in the auction for licenses for third generation serives, the National Telecommunication Commission, or NTC, said Tuesday. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI CABINET APPROVES MOF PLAN TO SELL ITS SHARES IN THAI ESSO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Cabinet Tuesday approved the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's plan to divest its 7.3% stake in Esso PCL for THB1.7 billion, deputy government spokesman Watchara Kanikar said. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QANTAS AIRWAYS JULY PASSENGER NUMBERS UP 9.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its passenger numbers rose 9.1% in July from a year ago. (published 2347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANEKA TAMBANG 1H NET MORE THAN TRIPLES TO IDR756.30 BLN ON LOWER COST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold and nickel producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that first-half net profit more than tripled, mostly because of lower cost of sales. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBE ASIATIQUE REALTY IPO PLAN GETS APPROVAL FROM PSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Globe Asiatique Realty Holdings Corp's plan to conduct an initial public offering that could raise as much as PHP3.39 billion for the property developer has been approved by the Philippine Stock Exchange, the PSE said Monday. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONTEX TO COMPENSATE INVESTORS FOR IPO PROSPECTUS STATEMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese clothing maker Hontex International Holdings Co. said Monday it plans to compensate investors after its audit committee found that statements appearing in the company's initial public offering prospectus for its Hong Kong listing in December are unreliable. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP PLANS TO DOUBLE ASIA DESKS IN NEXT YEAR FROM CURRENT 13 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to double its Asian desks in the next year from 13 now, with most of the new desks in Latin America and Africa, as the bank ramps up its coverage globally to match the increasing globalization of its Asian clients. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES FALL; TECH PLAYS DOWN, TOKYO HIT BY STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were lower Tuesday, as regional technology stocks fell while the Tokyo market dropped sharply as investors continued to fret about the yen's strength. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA IMPOSES ANTISUBSIDY TARIFF ON CHICKEN PRODUCTS FROM U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has imposed an antisubsidy tariff of 4.0% to 30.3% on chicken products imported from the U.S. from Monday, the Ministry of Commerce said in a statement following a final ruling on the tariff level. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA MIN: INDONESIA SEEKING IDR22T COMPENSATION FROM PTTEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia is seeking IDR22 trillion in compensation from Thailand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Exploration & Production PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  for alleged damage from an oil leak last year, a minister said Tuesday. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTAN PSO TO DEFER MORE GASOIL, LSFO CARGOES FOR AUG-SEP -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistan State Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will likely defer imports of as many as five gasoil and four low-sulfur fuel-oil cargoes in August and September, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: SMX GOLD BETTER THAN COMEX FOR ASIA HEDGERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore Mercantile Exchange gold futures contract, which starts trading Tuesday, is likely to become a popular hedging tool for Asian physical-market participants, a senior exchange official said. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA AUGUST COAL CONSUMPTION RISES; STOCKS SUFFICIENT -AGENCY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coal consumption by China's key power plants rose this month due to hot summer weather, but coal stocks remain sufficient as supply is stable, China's top economic planning agency said Tuesday. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECUADOR PREPARES TO SIGN FOR $1 BILLION LOAN FROM CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government of Ecuador and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will sign in the coming hours a $1 billion loan agreement, a high-level government official told Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 2258 GMT Monday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CNNC: CHINA URANIUM, CHINA-AFRICA FUND TO EXPLORE URANIUM IN AFRICA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Uranium Corp. has signed an agreement with the China-Africa Development Fund, or CADFund, to develop uranium resources in Africa, parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Nuclear Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE SMX STARTS TRADING EURO-BRENT, WTI CONTRACTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore Mercantile Exchange started Tuesday trading of its prompt West Texas Intermediate crude contract at $74.14 a barrel and its euro-denominated Brent crude contract at EUR61 a barrel. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE SMX DECEMBER GOLD CONTRACT STARTS TRADING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore Mercantile Exchange started trading its December gold futures contract Tuesday. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE EXCHANGE PLANS METALS FUTURES CONTRACTS WITH LME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it plans to introduce metals futures contracts following a partnership deal it struck with the London Metal Exchange. (published 0020 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN LNG IMPORTS FROM RUSSIA MORE THAN TRIPLED IN JAN-JUL -MOF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's imports of liquefied natural gas from Russia more than tripled from a year earlier to 3.5 million metric tons in the first seven months of this year, data from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANTAM-SHOWA DENKO JV APPOINTS CONSORTIUM TO BUILD ITS ALUMINA PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Indonesia Chemical Alumina, a joint venture company formed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Antam, and Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Showa Denko K.K\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., signed Tuesday a $450 million deal with a consortium that will build its chemical-grade alumina plant. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 2010-11 WHEAT EXPORTS FORECAST 15 MLN TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exports from the 2010-11 Australian wheat crop will likely fall somewhat short of projections by the U.S. Department of Agriculture, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported Tuesday, reflecting a difference in production estimates by the two organizations. (published 0555 GMT) [ 31-08-10 0709GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100831e68v000ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
