\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 809 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2010\par 07:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION EDGES UP, MAY STALL AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's industrial production edged up in July due to higher output in the general machinery and chemicals sectors, but the slight rise is unlikely to dispel concerns that gains could stall in the months ahead as the country's economy slows. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER DEFENDS BOJ STEP; THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister defended the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday from criticism that its latest policy step was too modest to halt the yen's rise, suggesting the minister may refrain from demanding more monetary easing for some time. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT NARROWEST SINCE 1989 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia posted its smallest current account deficit in more than 20 years in the second quarter as the mining boom continues to reshape the economy, putting it on the path of virtually unrivalled prosperity against a slackening global backdrop. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT BEATS FORECASTS; OUTLOOK CLOUDY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stronger than expected growth in South Korea's July industrial production showed yet again that the recovery remains solid despite increased external uncertainties, but the data also suggest the country won't be free from the slower growth momentum in the U.S. and China for much longer. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA PBOC, HK'S MING PAO DENY BOND-LOSS RUMORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denied rumors Monday that the bank's chief had fled after posting big bond losses, while a Hong Kong newspaper denied being the source of the rumors. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ GOVERNMENT MOVING SWIFTLY TO REPAY ALL SOUTH CANTERBURY FINANCE DEPOSITORS -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government is taking steps to swiftly repay the money owed to South Canterbury depositors under the Crown Retail Deposit Guarantee, Finance Minister Bill English said Tuesday. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RBA SAYS BANKS COULD GO OUTSIDE SYSTEM IF REGULATION OVERDOSED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cracking down too hard in the area of banking regulation could be counterproductive as banks would then look to take risk outside of the system, Guy Debelle, assistant governor of financial markets at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Tuesday. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN BANKS STOCKPILING GOVERNMENT DEBT AHEAD OF BASEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian banks have already begun to stockpile government debt and will continue to do so ahead of regulatory requirements that may even be a few years away, said the head of group funding and execution for Commonwealth Bank Australia Tuesday. (published 0427 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ JULY DWELLING CONSENT DATA SUGGEST MARKET WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of residential building permits excluding apartments fell, suggesting the property market is anemic and leading economists to further question whether the economy is sufficiently robust for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to again raise the official cash rate. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA IMPOSES ANTISUBSIDY TARIFF ON CHICKEN PRODUCTS FROM U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has imposed an antisubsidy tariff of 4.0% to 30.3% on chicken products imported from the U.S. from Monday, the Ministry of Commerce said in a statement following a final ruling on the tariff level. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA MAY RAISE IDR3 TLN-IDR6 TLN VIA SAMURAI BOND ISSUE -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia may raise between IDR3 trillion and IDR6 trillion through Samurai bond issuance expected later this year, Finance Minister Agus Martowardoyo said Tuesday. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RENHE COMMERCIAL HOLDINGS SEEKS TO PAY AROUND 13% ON 5.5-YEAR DOLLAR BOND -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Renhe Commercial Holdings Co. is seeking to pay a yield of around 13% on a proposed 5.5-year U.S. dollar bond, a person familiar with the offering said Tuesday. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CFTC UNVEILS FINAL RULES FOR RETAIL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal futures regulators finalized new rules for the retail \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market late Monday, but they backed away from their original proposal to place strict limits on the amount of borrowed funds retail \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors can use. (published 0213 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: WHITE HOUSE: MORE ECONOMIC STIMULUS MEASURES COMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama on Monday said his economic team is working to identify new measures to stimulate U.S. growth as part of a "full-scale attack" to strengthen the lackluster economy. (published 2221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =CHARTING ASIA: AUSSIE MAY RISE TO US$0.9082, US$0.9221 N/T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar jumped 0.37 percent against the U.S. dollar Tuesday on upbeat Australian data, and looks set to advance further in coming days. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: JAPAN RUNNING OUT OF OPTIONS TO ANCHOR YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's monetary-easing measures took no wind from the yen's sails Monday, calling into question the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ability to halt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's climb toward an all-time high against the dollar. (published 1920 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-08-10 0506GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100831e68v000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
