\par\par \b \uc2 Q+A-UPDATE 1-Will  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano   \par \uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2010\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds link to interview with former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The yen's surge to a 15-year high against the dollar is threatening Japan's export-reliant economy, hitting the Nikkei share average and prompting Japanese authorities to consider unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years.\par \par \uc2 While sources have told Reuters the government is not ruling out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders and analysts believe that the drop in the dollar/yen rate <JPY=> would have to become much more volatile or deeper for the authorities to take action.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rise is adding to deflationary pressures on the Japanese economy, and the toll on shares of exporters has driven the Nikkei <.N225> down 16 percent -- making it one of the worst performing markets in the world this year next to China and Greece.\par \par \uc2 WHAT WOULD PROVOKE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 A sharp drop in dollar/yen, perhaps 1 to 2 percent or more in a single day towards the 80 yen level or below, is seen as the most likely scenario that would prompt Japan to stick its neck out and buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 Such an abrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move would likely drag the Nikkei down even further, piling up pressure on the government to take action. \uc2 Suzuki Motors\uc2  CEO \uc2 Osamu Suzuki\uc2  said last week that he hoped the government would hear "our cries of desperation".\par \par \uc2 From last week both Prime Minister Naoto Kan and Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda started to hint at possible action to counter yen strength, raising speculation that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be just around the corner. [ID:nTOE67U03E]\par \par \uc2 Some traders think a fall in the dollar/yen rate below last week's 15-year low of 83.58 yen would be enough to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But others believe the yen's rise would likely need to accelerate for authorities to justify such a move.\par \par \uc2 Market volatility gauges have been subdued, and some measures of realised volatility are up only modestly after having dropped to their lowest levels since 2007, just before the global financial crisis began.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a package on the yen click: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nef47n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nef47n}}}\par \par \uc2 Interview with ex-BOJ board member Mizuno [ID:nTKF106989]\par \par \uc2 More stories on the Japanese economy [ID:nECONJP]\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on dollar/yen implied and realised\par \par \uc2 volatilities, click on: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/bux96n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/bux96n}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Japan may thus have a hard time convincing its G7 partners about the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just when they are calling on China to make its yuan <CNY=CFXS> more flexible to ease global imbalances.\par \par \uc2 Any attempt to cheapen the yen could run counter to U.S. President Barack Obama's plan to double U.S. exports, especially with mid-term congressional elections approaching in November, raising diplomatic obstacles to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Many market players think Tokyo will likely hold fire unless the dollar/yen rate slips below its record low of 79.75 yen.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's decision on Monday to expand its fixed-rate fund supply scheme to 30 trillion yen from 20 trillion yen, and to launch a new six-month loan \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in addition to an existing three-month scheme, has done little to curb the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 The onus may then fall on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen keeps on strengthening. The finance ministry makes any decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act as the ministry's agent.\par \par \uc2 HAS \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  ABANDONED ITS OLD \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONIST\b0 \highlight\uc2  WAYS?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not as quick to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it used to be, partly due to a seeming shift of views within the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2004, when a 15-month yen-selling spree came to an end. During that period, they sold 35 trillion yen ($414.1 billion), the equivalent of more than one-third of the annual budget.\par \par \uc2 Even a rare G7 statement between meetings in October 2008, which singled out yen volatility and was seen as giving \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  approval to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , did not tempt Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts also think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would amount to little more than a drop in the ocean, since the driving force behind the yen's rise is mounting worry that the U.S. economy is headed for a double-dip recession and the Federal Reserve may boost quantitative easing -- driving down U.S. Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 In terms of volume, the amount of dollar buying in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only be a small fraction of trading on the world's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, where $1.7 trillion changes hands in London alone each day, on average.\par \par \uc2 In the 2003-2004 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the score card was mixed at best as the yen continued to gain gradually during the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Fear of losses from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may make make Tokyo reluctant. The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to curb strength in the Swiss franc this year, has faced criticism for losing $13.6 billion on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1=84.53 Yen) (Editing by Nathan Layne)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Q+A, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|NAT|J|SI|RBN|UKI|AUF|ND|ABN|M|E|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100831e68v000gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
