\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rises, heads to 4th straight monthly gain vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2010\par 02:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Market tests \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Dollar/yen on track for fourth monthly gain\par \par \uc2 * Euro hits record low against Swiss franc (Adds comments, details; changes byline)\par \par \uc2 By Vivianne Rodrigues and Aleksandra Michalska\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The yen rose and was on track for its fourth consecutive monthly advance against the dollar on Tuesday, its longest winning streak in 19 months, as investors shrugged off Japan's latest easing move.\par \par \uc2 Demand for the safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose in the past month as U.S. Treasury yields tumbled amid mounting signs the economic recovery in the United States was faltering.\par \par \uc2 The rapid advance, which pushed the yen to a 15-year high this month, prompted Japanese authorities to announce measures on Monday to curb the yen's strength to protect the country's exports. For details, see [ID:nTOE67S01V]\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves as a symbolic gesture that will do little to halt the climb. They said that short of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the yen is bound to test its all-time high of 79.75 yen set in April 1995, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 "The policy action by the BoJ isn't going to change the market's mood. It would probably take \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shake things up a bit," said Vassili Serebriakov, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 But Serebriakov and other analysts cautioned that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have limited impact. "We're not even sure that (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would cause a sustained reversal of yen strength," he said.\par \par \uc2 Japan last sold yen in the markets to weaken it in March 2004, with mixed results.\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading, the dollar was down 0.8 percent at 83.96 yen <JPY=>, not far from its 15-year low of 83.58 set on electronic trading platform EBS last week. The euro fell 0.6 percent to 106.50 yen <EURJPY=>.\par \par \uc2 "The yen has a little further to go," said Daniel Katzive, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York. "We think dollar/yen can get down to 82 in the near term."\par \par \uc2 He said that with global benchmarks yields near or at record lows, Japanese investors would need more incentive to take risk in foreign markets, helping sustain demand for the yen.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda repeated on Tuesday that the government would take decisive action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- usually seen as code for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- when necessary.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  RISK\par \par \uc2 The dollar has fallen almost 3 percent against the yen this month and is down more than 9 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Traders say Japanese authorities are expected to buy the dollar against the yen if the dollar slides 3-4 yen in one day.\par \par \uc2 The yen could also face potential buyback pressure in cross trades such as euro/yen and Aussie/yen, which have attracted some interest because of their larger yield differentials.\par \par \uc2 U.S. economic data this week, including Friday's nonfarm payrolls report, could push the yen higher if they show further deterioration in the economy and weigh on bond yields, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar did not react to the release of minutes of the Federal Reserve's August meeting as it only reinforced the view the Fed is ready to provide additional policy stimulus if the economic outlook weakens.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro rose 0.2 percent to $1.2684 <EUR=>, but it slumped to a record low 1.2850 francs on electronic trading platform EBS <EURCHF=EBS>. (Additional reporting by Nick Olivari and Steven C. Johnson in New York; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|UKI|CANT|AUF|J|Z|ABX|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100831e68v0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
