\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2010\par 06:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ TAKES EASING ACTION; EXTENDS DURATION OF LOW INTEREST-RATE LOANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided in a hastily convened policy board meeting Monday to loosen monetary policy further by lengthening the duration of low interest-rate loans available to the money market. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN, BOJ GOVERNOR SHIRAKAWA TO MEET MON AFTERNOON -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Prime Minister Naoto Kan said he will meet with Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa on Monday afternoon, the Nikkei reported. (published 0058 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE UNVEILS MORE PROPERTY INVESTMENT CURBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's government Monday introduced new curbs against property speculation that has pushed prices to record highs in the city-state, with regulators worried that the market could head south as quickly should the economy slow. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND JULY TRADE DEFICIT WIDER THAN MARKET EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's trade balance swung into deficit in July from a surplus in June, driven by increased imports of cars, petroleum and fertilizer and a seasonal decline in exports of milk, one of the country's main products. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN NEW HOME SALES FALL 7% IN JULY VS JUNE - HIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian new home sales fell 7% in July from June, the third consecutive monthly decline and further confirmation that higher interest rates are eroding demand in the sector. (published 0058 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ NBNZ AUG BUSINESS CONFIDENCE +16.4% VS +27.9% JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's business confidence eased in August from July on increasing concerns about the tepid nature of the economic recovery, a leading survey showed Monday. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY RAISE RATES 25 BPS THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may hike its policy interest rate by 25 basis points before the year ends to cool the domestic economy, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Monday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FACES POLICY DILEMMAS, SHOULD KEEP POLICY STABLE - PEOPLE'S DAILY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China faces multiple "dilemmas" in macroeconomic policy as growth is slowing but inflation expectations remain strong, an editorial in the People's Daily said Monday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK ECONOMY TO SLOW SHARPLY OVER MEDIUM TERM - BCC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pace of the U.K.'s economic growth will slow sharply over the medium term as the coalition government's tough measures to reduce the deficit set in, the British Chambers of Commerce said Sunday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK FIRST TIME HOME BUYERS SET TO SINK TO NEW LOW - RIGHTMOVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The proportion of first time home buyers in the U.K. is expected to sink to a new low over the coming year, accentuating the challenges facing the U.K. housing market, a survey by property website Rightmove released Monday finds. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WOULD FACE POWERFUL CROSS CURRENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does dive into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to try to quell strength in the yen, it will find itself struggling against some strong cross currents. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HEARD ON THE STREET: CHINA'S LOOMING PEOPLE PROBLEM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If having too small a population doesn't seem like a pressing problem for China, think again. (published 1636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =US MONEY WEEK AHEAD: TREASURY INVESTORS SEEK SIGNS OF EASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury investors searching for clues about whether policymakers may redouble their efforts to help the economy will zero in on next week's jobs report, a possible turning point for the bond market and a potential catalyst for much lower yields. (published 2200 GMT) [ 30-08-10 0402GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100830e68u00081\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
