\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 7-BOJ eases policy, government hints at  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 873 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2010\par 08:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * BOJ eases monetary policy, impact questioned\par \par \uc2 * Shirakawa meets PM, ministers decide on econ steps\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may test govt resolve on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Govt signals possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Markets disappointed BOJ stopped short of aggressive steps (Adds government signals on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan boosted its cheap loan scheme on Monday, bowing to government pressure for action to protect a fragile recovery by curbing the yen's rise, while cabinet ministers signalled they may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen surged more than 1 percent against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  beefed up the supply of fixed-rate loans to banks, a move investors saw as a symbolic gesture that will do little to halt a climb in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that hurts exports and may prolong deflation.\par \par \uc2 Government officials, increasingly alarmed by the yen's rise that took it to a 15-year high against the dollar last week, have tried to talk down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while leaning on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help by further relaxing its policy.\par \par \uc2 Now, the BOJ's cautious move at an emergency meeting held a week ahead of a scheduled review put the ball back in the government's court and market players may test its resolve to back its words with yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Today's move is not a bold move," said Simon Wong, regional economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen continues to appreciate, say it appreciates beyond the 80 level, that could trigger more direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point."\par \par \uc2 In a statement after a meeting on economic steps to help keep the recovery on track, cabinet ministers said the government would watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves carefully and take "decisive action" as needed -- a phrase seen as code for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is facing a rise in the yen and there are concerns about a slowdown in overseas economies," Prime Minister Naoto Kan told a meeting of ministers with economic portfolios.\par \par \uc2 Japan's economic growth slowed to a crawl in the second quarter as exports to the United States and China ebbed and stimulus-driven consumption petered out. Analysts expect growth to slow further later this year, with the yen's surge to a 15-year high against the dollar adding to the pain.\par \par \uc2 MARKET PLAYERS DISAPPOINTED\par \par \uc2 Market players were disappointed that the BOJ failed to act more aggressively and, for example, increase Japanese government bond purchases or cut its benchmark rate fom 0.1 percent to zero.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa told a news conference the current level of bond buying was appropriate, but hinted at possible further action by raising the possibility of a downgrade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic forecasts.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rebound pulled the Nikkei share average off its peaks and helped Japanese government bond futures bounce back from an early plunge.\par \par \uc2 Kan, whose Democratic Party swept to power a year ago but was thrashed in a July upper house poll, is keen to show that he is doing something about the economy ahead of a challenge from powerbroker Ichiro Ozawa in a Sept. 14 party leadership vote that could split the party.\par \par \uc2 Kan, his fiscal options constrained by a public debt worth twice the size of the economy, said the government would use 920 billion yen ($10.78 billion) in reserve funds to pay for steps that include jobs-related measures and deregulation.\par \par \uc2 But he added that an extra budget for the current fiscal year to March 31 would be compiled if needed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone if it were to step in to curb yen gains, as its Group of Seven counterparts, happy with the benefits to exports from their weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are in no mood for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, will not have much effect in weakening the yen unless backed by aggressive monetary easing, traders say.\par \par \uc2 In Monday's move, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased the volume of money available to banks under its fixed-rate fund supply \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 30 trillion yen from 20 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2 It also put in place a six-month fund \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in addition to the three-month loan programme already in place.\par \par \uc2 Of the 30 trillion yen, 10 trillion yen will be the six-month fund \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ said. The decision was by an 8-1 vote, with board member Miyako Suda dissenting.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as widely expected, maintained its overnight core rate target at 0.1 percent by a unanimous vote.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ launched the funding scheme, which offers loans at 0.1 percent, in December. That failed to boost bank lending but helped to push the yen further away from a November high.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ last eased monetary policy in March, when it doubled the size of the fixed-rate fund supply tool to 20 trillion yen. ($1=85.37 Yen) (Writing by Leika Kihara and Linda Sieg; Additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto, Chisa Fujioka and Yoko Nishikawa; Editing by Edmund Klamann and Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 7, PIX)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100829e68t0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
