\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dlr rises on report Japan PM to speak on yen\b0\par\par\uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2010\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Japan PM to brief media Friday on yen steps-Kyodo\par \par \uc2 * Japan exporters seen waiting to sell dollar on rallies\par \par \uc2 * Wariness about possible Japan steps may limit yen rise\par \par \uc2 * Traders await Bernanke's speech at Fed gathering\par \par \uc2 * Yen may scale record high in 2010 despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervent\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 27 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the yen on Friday, trimming earlier losses due to wariness on possible measures from Japanese authorities to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 Prompting these jitters was a Kyodo news agency report saying Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan will hold a news conference on Friday on the government's steps to cope with a recent surge in the yen. [ID:nTKZ006503]\par \par \uc2 Separately, Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda reiterated that the government will take appropriate action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary. [ID:nTKX006956]\par \par \uc2 "The yen did dip a little bit, but I think market players were already bracing for this type of news," said Yuji Matsuura, joint general manager for \uc2 Aozora Bank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  & derivatives trading group.\par \par \uc2 Any gains in the greenback could turn out to be limited, with Japanese exporters likely to be waiting to sell the dollar on any rallies, Matsuura said.\par \par \uc2 The yen may also get a lift if Kan does not unveil any concrete steps to curb the yen's rise, Matsuura added.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was up 0.3 percent against the yen from late U.S. trading on Thursday at 84.71 yen <JPY=>.\par \par \uc2 The greenback pulled up from an intraday low of 84.27 yen as the media report on Kan's news conference sparked short-squeezing in dollar/yen, a senior trader at a big Japanese bank said.\par \par \uc2 But the pair was was still not that far away from a 15-year low of 83.58 yen hit on trading platform EBS earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Another focus is what Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke may say on the U.S. economy when he speaks later on Friday at the annual Federal Reserve conference in Jackson Hole, Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 Investors will be watching to see whether the Fed's views on the economy have become bleaker since its policy meeting earlier in August. [ID:nN25199098]\par \par \uc2 "In addition, the market will closely watch for hints of further expansion to the balance sheet. Jackson Hole has not traditionally been a venue for major policy statements, but we do not exclude this possibility," analysts at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve announced plans earlier this month to boost a flagging economy by reinvesting money from maturing mortgage bonds in government debt.\par \par \uc2 Market players say the Fed's pledge to maintain asset purchases and shift to Treasuries suggests it may boost the size of its already massive $2.3 trillion balance sheet if the economy loses momentum.\par \par \uc2 The euro inched up 0.1 percent to $1.2728 <EUR=>. It dipped to a six-week low of $1.2588 earlier this week, partly due to a renewed focus on fiscal woes among some peripheral euro zone countries. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ PDF on Japan's yen puzzle:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nef47n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nef47n}}}\uc2  Q+A-Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen's rise?\par \par \uc2 [ID:nTOE67O07Q] BOJ FOCUS on chance of monetary easing\par \par \uc2 [ID:nTOE67N07Z] Why the yen may remain strong\par \par \uc2 [ID:nTOE67B078] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 WILL YEN HIT RECORD PEAK?\par \par \uc2 Despite the risk of possible action by Japanese authorities to curb yen strength such as yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or monetary easing by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some traders and investors say the yen could test a record high of 79.75 yen to the dollar, hit in April 1995, later this year.\par \par \uc2 The fate of the yen will depend on the overall trend of the U.S. economy rather than the possibility of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Michiharu Maeda, general manager of Dai-ichi's separate account management division told Reuters in an interview on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The current mood of testing a record high of 79.75 (against the dollar) will stay in place in the near term," Maeda said.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that there is a big chance of the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by itself ... but the impact could be limited as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts could result in creating more chances for the market to sell (the dollar against the yen)," Maeda said.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts think solo yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities would amount to little more than a drop in the ocean, since the driving force behind the yen's rise is mounting worry that the U.S. economy is headed for a double-dip recession and the Federal Reserve may boost quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 A euro zone source familiar with the situation said on Thursday that joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rise of the yen is not likely, and that it is more realistic to expect Japan to act alone. [ID:nLDE67P16B]\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Wayne Cole in Sydney; Chikafumi Hodo and Rika Otsuka in Tokyo; Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|GNN|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100827e68r000eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
