\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Japan PM Kan vows firm moves against strong yen\b0\par\par\uc2 961 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2010\par 02:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Japan PM says to meet BOJ governor after Aug. 30\par \par \uc2  * Dollar edges higher after Kan says to take firm measures\par \par \uc2  * BOJ under pressure for further action to beat deflation\par \par \uc2  * Japan July core CPI falls 1.1 pct y/y, matches forecast\par \par \uc2  * Deflation unlikely to ease much in weak economy -analysts  (Rewrites with PM Kan's comments, details)\par \par \uc2  By Stanley White and Rie Ishiguro\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 27 (Reuters) - Japan's prime minister said on Friday he will take firm measures on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed and will meet the Bank of Japan governor, increasing the possibility the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ease policy soon as it confronts a surging yen.\par \par \uc2  The yen edged lower after Kan's remarks as Japanese policymakers struggle over how to put a cap on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hit a 15-year high against the dollar this week and threatens to derail an export-led recovery.\par \par \uc2  The ruling Democratic Party's options on fiscal policy are limited due to the country's large debt burden, so it is leaning on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease policy to help the economy.\par \par \uc2  "There are investors who are expecting the Japanese authorities to take some measures if the yen appreciates sharply," said Mitsuru Sahara, chief manager for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives trading at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2  "It's possible that the government's stimulus steps and the BOJ's easing measures will be announced together, even before its next meeting," he said, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate review on Sept. 6-7.\par \par \uc2  "There's a growing view that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could even conduct solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen rises sharply."\par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa is scheduled to attend the Federal Reserve's seminar in Jackson Hole, Wyoming, until Aug. 30, and Kan said he would meet Shirakawa after he returns to Japan.   <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic of CPI trends         {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/pum57n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/pum57n}}}\par \par \uc2 Package of Reuters reports on the yen\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nef47n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nef47n}}}\par \par \uc2 More stories on the Japanese economy            [ID:nECONJP]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2  Kan said the government would outline measures on Aug. 31 to support the economy and grapple with the strong yen.\par \par \uc2  "Excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves can harm the economy and the financial system," he told reporters after visiting a small factory in the Tokyo suburbs. "We will take firm measures when needed."\par \par \uc2  The fate of any economic package could be complicated, however, by a ruling Democratic Party leadership vote on Sept. 14, in which party powerbroker Ichiro Ozawa is challenging Kan.\par \par \uc2  The dollar rose slightly to 84.82 yen <JPY=> after Kan's comments, near its high for the session, but remained below the closely watched 85 mark and not far from a 15-year low of 83.58 yen hit on trading platform EBS earlier this week.\par \par \uc2  Sources say the BOJ is considering easing policy further at its upcoming rate review, or even before that, but it is expected to opt for only a minor tweak of its funding framework instead of bolder steps such as increasing its government bond purchases. [ID:nTOE67Q04C]\par \par \uc2  Analysts say such a modest step would do little to slow the yen's rise or bolster the fragile economy.\par \par \uc2  BOJ HESITANT\par \par \uc2  Debt markets are already pricing in the chance of a BOJ easing. With short-term rates already very low, investors are pushing down the longer end of the curve, although the yield curve steepened on Friday as banks sold super-long bonds to take profits. [JP/]\par \par \uc2  The BOJ is hesitant to return to full-blown quantitative easing since the policy, which involves flooding markets with extra cash under a liquidity target, had little effect in beating deflation when it was in place until March 2006.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March 2004, when it ended a 15-month 35 trillion yen selling spree aimed at rescuing an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  The firmer yen also threatens to delay Japan's exit from deflation, putting further pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act.\par \par \uc2  Japan's core consumer price index (CPI), which includes oil products but excludes fresh food prices, fell 1.1 percent in July from a year earlier, data from the internal affairs ministry showed on Friday, matching the median market forecast. It was slightly bigger than a 1.0 percent drop in June. [JPCPI=ECI]\par \par \uc2  The core-core inflation index, which excludes food and energy prices and is similar to the core index used in the United States, fell 1.5 percent in July from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2  "Given the yen's gains, exports will slump temporarily and slow Japan's economic recovery. Japan will thus remain in deflation for another two to three years," said Takeshi Minami, chief economist at Norinchukin Research Institute.\par \par \uc2  "The BOJ may expand its fund-supply tool next month, but the effect on short-term interest rates will be limited. It needs to take bolder steps to beat deflation and the strong yen, such as increasing outright government bond purchases, although that's unlikely to happen soon."\par \par \uc2  The BOJ has justified holding off on aggressive measures to beat deflation with its forecast that consumer prices will turn positive in the fiscal year ending in March 2012.\par \par \uc2  The government steps due at the end of the month are likely to delay the end of subsidies on purchases of energy-efficient electronics.\par \par \uc2  But any positive effect on the economy will be limited as spending under the stimulus plan will be small and any measures taken by the BOJ will be minor and cosmetic, analysts say.  (Writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Edmund Klamann & Kim Coghill)    \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|G|RBN|J|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|DNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100827e68r0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
