\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Modest Losses For Dollar Following Jobless Claims\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sam Mamudi  \par \uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2010\par 19:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar eased slightly Thursday against the euro and the yen, after U.S. initial jobless claims showed a larger-than-expected decline for last week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index (DXY), which measures the greenback against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stood at 82.946, down from 83.298 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is down against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with broader financial markets more stable in today's trading, although it is perhaps an uneasy calm that is prevailing across markets," analysts at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  said. "The gains in global equity markets appear to be more of a consolidation after recent large declines, rather than reflecting truly bullish sentiment."\par \par \uc2 The Labor Department said the number of people filing first-time claims for unemployment benefits fell 31,000 to 473,000, marking the first weekly decline in four and exceeding a decrease forecast at 5,000.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, and to a greater extent the yen, tend to lose ground when investors are more open to buying equities and other assets perceived as carrying greater risk.\par \par \uc2 Against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar (CUR_USDYEN) bought \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A584.62, down from \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A584.80 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Masaaki Shirakawa, the head of the Bank of Japan, will attend the Jackson Hole \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conference this week. The top central banker's plan to attend the conference "heightened market attention on the possibility of Japanese action," with Shirakawa expected to have an opportunity to speak to Bernanke and others, according to analysts at Action Economics.\par \par \uc2 Still, if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen's rise, it will most likely have to go it alone as most countries are not keen to see the yen weaken, which will make Japanese exports more competitive on price, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without international support will have to fulfill two conditions to be successful: First, it will have to be conducted within a time window where there are no important fundamental data releases. Weak U.S. or Chinese data can undermine the JPY weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effect," they wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 The euro (CUR_EURUSD) changed hands at $1.2704 in recent action, up from $1.2651 in late North American trading Wednesday. The euro (CUR_EURYEN) traded at 107.50 yen, up slightly from \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A5107.27.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lending and money-supply figures for July had little bearing on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, but showed that private-sector loan growth picked up some momentum. A weak overall tone to the lending data raised warning flags over the strength of the region's recovery in coming months, economists said.\par \par \uc2 "The news on the credit front does indicate some improvement, but it is occurring at such a glacial pace that it will likely force the ECB to maintain its ultra-loose monetary posture at least through the end of the year," said Boris Schlossberg, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at GFT.\par \par \uc2 Strategists at KBC Bank said investors remain uncertain about how to trade the euro against the dollar. That's because investors don't know whether they should trade global aversion to risk, which tends to boost the greenback on safe-haven flows, or aversion to the United States and the dollar due to growing signs of a steep slowdown in U.S. economic activity, they added.\par \par \uc2 "The jury is still out on this issue, but we have the impression that downside in euro/U.S. dollar is becoming more difficult," KBC strategists commented.\par \par \uc2 Participants across financial markets await Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's speech Friday in Jackson Hole, Wyo.\par \par \uc2 "The risk at this stage is the Fed cannot satisfy market expectations, even though they have already shifted policy away from balance-sheet contraction," said Geoffrey Yu, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 . "That uncertainty could help the dollar at the current juncture and the spotlight is getting more intense on Fed Chairman Bernanke's upcoming speech with every negative data print."\par \par \uc2 The British pound (CUR_GBPUSD) also firmed against the dollar, trading at $1.5540, up from $1.5445.\par \par \uc2 The Confederation of British Industry on Thursday said its latest survey found annualized growth in retail sales volumes for August showed the fastest increase since April 2007. [ 08-26-10 1323ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020100826e68q0005h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
