\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Joint yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  unlikely -euro zone source\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2010\par 13:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Solo BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely than joint action -source\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  jittery about yen but U.S. and Europe less so -source\par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 By Gabriella Bruschi\par \par \uc2 MILAN, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rise of the yen is not likely, and it is more realistic to expect Japan to act alone, a euro zone source familiar with the situation said on Thursday. The yen hit 15-year highs against the dollar earlier this week but has since pulled back on mounting speculation that Japanese authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since March 2004 to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 "At present it seems more realistic to see a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the Japanese authorities," the source, who spoke on condition of anonymity, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment I see a lot of jitters in Japan, but I don't see anything similar in the United States or in the euro zone," the source said. "Clearly the current levels of their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not regarded as being that negative."\par \par \uc2 The source did not entirely rule out co-ordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, and said that such a case would most likely involve the Federal Reserve and each \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acting on its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The main focus is the dollar/yen, so one could think that the United States could possibly act with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . An ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro/yen seems more difficult, also because the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more of an impact for the U.S. than for the euro zone economy."\par \par \uc2 "Even a possible euro/yen level of 100 should not trouble the ECB," the source added.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose slightly to 84.60 yen on Thursday, having moved in a narrow range of 84.49-84.90 yen all day. Earlier this week it hit a 15-year low of 83.58 yen.\par \par \uc2 The euro also pushed slightly higher against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 107.52 yen, extending its recovery from a nine-year low of 105.44 yen hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Markets have been rife with speculation that the Bank of Japan will ease monetary policy further before its regular rate review on Sept. 6-7 at an emergency meeting.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa will attend the Kansas City Federal Reserve's conference in Jackson Hole in the United States this week, and analysts say that an emergency meeting is less likely to take place while he is away.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa, who chairs the BOJ's policy meetings, will return to Tokyo on Aug. 30.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, Japan's deputy finance minister Motohisa Ikeda said the yen's rapid rise was undesirable for the economy.\par \par \uc2 He added that he believed the Bank of Japan would "make an appropriate decision on monetary policy based on market and economic trends."\par \par \uc2 The euro zone source familiar with the situation noted that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks had been rare in the past 10 years, adding it was "a very complex \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that requires good agreement on what is the right exchange rate." (Writing by Silvia Aloisi; editing by Patrick Graham and Hugh Lawson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YEN/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100826e68q000sr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
