\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA MARKETS: Yen Eases On Hopes Japan Will Act\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2010\par 06:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 By V. Phani Kumar\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen beat a retreat from 15-year highs Wednesday on strengthened hopes that the government would swing into action to protect the economy from the adverse effects of a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to stem the unit's rally.\par \par \uc2 Expectation that Japanese authorities might make coordinated attempts to protect the nation's exporters pushed the U.S. dollar (CUR_USDYEN) to 84.38 yen in Asian trading hours Wednesday from a 15-year low of 83.57 yen overnight in New York. The euro, meanwhile, was buying 106.78 yen from 105.41 yen overnight.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's rise came after Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda was quoted as saying in reports that he will monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements with grave concern and that he will work closely with the Bank of Japan in dealing with the yen's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Additional monetary easing measures by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be on the cards if the yen rises further against the dollar, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Weaker-than-expected U.S. economic data could lower the [U.S. dollar-yen exchange rate] range to 82-83 [yen]. In this case, we think the BOJ would not only increase its fixed-rate lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would also take bold additional easing measures. Now we think an extraordinary BOJ meeting is also a possibility," Nomura Securities strategist Yunosuke Ikeda wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The yen's fall Wednesday came amid reports that Finance Minister Noda and Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan were meeting to discuss the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Japanese exporters continued to fall Wednesday, stretching the benchmark Nikkei Stock Average's loss-making run to a fourth straight session. The Nikkei, which dropped below the psychologically important 9,000-point level and signaled the Japanese market's entry into bearish territory Tuesday, was down 1% in afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Nikon Corp\uc2 . (NINOY) dropped 1.4%, \uc2 Canon Inc\uc2 . (CAJ) shed 1.7%, and \uc2 Honda Motor Corp\uc2 . (HMC) lost 1.6% amid concerns exporters might miss their annual profit forecasts on the yen's strength. Several Japanese exporters have assumed an exchange rate of about 90 yen to the U.S. dollar and about 110 yen to the euro for their projections.\par \par \uc2 In wider Asian markets, Australia's S&P/ASX 200, China's Shanghai Composite and South Korea's Kospi each fell 1%, with Taiwan's Taiex dropping 1.9% and Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index slipping 0.2%, while India's Sensex dipped 0.1% in early trading.\par \par \uc2 The drop in shares came despite data released Wednesday showing Japan's export growth and trade surplus were stronger than expected in July. Preliminary figures released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Japan's monthly exports rose 23.5% from the year-earlier month, while the nation's trade surplus more than doubled to 804.2 billion yen ($9.55 billion) from 365.6 billion yen in May.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The overnight yen gains came as investors sought refuge in the relative safe haven of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after poor U.S. housing data and a \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgrade of Ireland's sovereign rating spurred risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the yen also rose as Noda, speaking at a news conference in Tokyo on Tuesday, declined to comment on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the government.\par \par \uc2 "The overnight session was characterized by a rather sharp round of risk aversion that started late yesterday, gained momentum during the European session and became entrenched following shockingly soft U.S. data," said Matthew Strauss, senior fixed-income and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , in emailed remarks to clients.\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown restraint so far from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the dollar against the yen's rise, some analysts said the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained.\par \par \uc2 "There is a high probability that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's industrial production data, to be released on Aug. 31, will fall far short of the market's forecast, which would help justify downward revisions to the BOJ's assessment," said Nomura's Yunosuke Ikeda.\par \par \uc2 "If the BOJ were to demonstrate a firm commitment to additional easing, it would likely help the government to gain the assent of [Group of Seven] nations for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ikeda said.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 25, 2010 00:17 ET (04:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100825e68p000p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
