\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If Yen Rises Too Far Or Too Fast - Sources\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2010\par 09:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:35 EDT *DJ  Zero Chance Of US Joining Any \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Source\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:35 EDT *DJ  Any \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Likely Limited To Smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Source\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:35 EDT *DJ  One-Day Dollar Fall Of Several Yen Could Prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Sources\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:35 EDT *DJ  Noda \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Comments Today Meant To Hint More Strongly \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Is Possible - Sources\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:36 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thinks US, Europe OK With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Smooth Sharp Moves - Sources\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:36 EDT *DJ  Some Concern That MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Once Started, Would Be Hard To Stop - Source\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:36 EDT *DJ  Yen Strength "Doesn't Make Much Sense" - Source\par \par \uc2 25 Aug 2010 03:55 EDT =DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  May \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  If Yen Rises Too Far Or Too Fast - Sources\par \par \uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market soon if the yen rises too quickly or too much, but any such action would be aimed at smoothing sharp market moves rather changing the yen's overall trend, said people familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 Japan would act on its own to combat the yen's surge to a 15-year high if it were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time since 2004, the people told Dow Jones Newswires. One person said there was a "zero" chance of the U.S. participating in any yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A decline in the dollar of several yen in a day could be a trigger for Japan to act, the people said.\par \par \uc2 One of the people said that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "never, ever said it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6895-7552; Takashi.Nakamichi@dowjones.com; Takeshi.Takeuchi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 25, 2010 03:55 ET (07:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100825e68p001n1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
