\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Yen Surges Across Board, Hits New 15-Year High Vs USD\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2010\par 10:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds detail, comments from Japanese finance minister) \par  \par    By Katie Martin \par    Of Dow Jones Newswires \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Japanese yen surged against a range of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, its gains accelerating after finance minister Yoshihiko Noda made no clear sign that authorities were preparing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reverse the move.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already pushed up to a fresh 15-year high against the dollar, an almost nine-year high against the euro, a three-month high against sterling, and a one-month high against the Australian dollar before Noda began a press conference in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 In it, Noda said he was watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closely, and noted that "disorderly" moves in the yen could hurt economic stability. However, he had no comment on the possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sell yen in its first direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2004.\par \par \uc2 The statement encouraged yet more yen buying in the market.\par \par \uc2 The dollar moved as low as Y84.45, while sterling sank under Y130 and the euro fell to Y106.35.\par \par \uc2 The push higher isn't a result of fresh positive sentiment on the Japanese economy, analysts say. Instead, it reflects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tendency to climb in times of general nervousness among investors. Growing concerns about the global economic recovery are fuelling such nerves right now.\par \par \uc2 In addition, declining chart patterns on the yen's movements have triggered pre-existing buy orders in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have widely bemoaned the strong yen of late, as it threatens exports by making Japanese goods more expensive abroad, and it exacerbates deflationary pressures by making imports cheaper.\par \par \uc2 -By Katie Martin, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9346; katie.martin@dowjones.com [ 24-08-10 0822GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100824e68o000ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
