.7%, \uc2 Alcoa\uc2  fell 3%, Caterpillar slipped 2.7%. \uc2 Medtronic\uc2  fell 11% on lowered earnings forecast. DJIA down 1.3%, Nasdaq off 1.7%, Philly Semicons fell 1.7%. Treasury market posted broad-based rally on demand for safer assets; 2-year yields down 1.2 bp at 0.47%, 10-year down 10.0 bp at 2.50%. Crude futures settled at lowest level in more than two months, falling on weakening equities markets, housing data. October Nymex Crude settled $1.42 lower at $71.63/bbl. December Comex gold rose $4.90 to $1,233.40/oz as investors fled to perceived safety of metal. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2336 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW likely to rise, possibly aim for a test above key 1,200 resistance vs 1,191.0 late yesterday on escalating concerns over global economic health after disappointing U.S. existing-home sales data overnight. Offshore players may opt for betting on stronger JPY/KRW as well, with JPY heading for fresh highs vs USD in broader market on increasing investor preference for safer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. Spot USD/KRW tipped to gap higher after 1-month NDFs last end around 1,197 in NY. Some resistance expected near 1,200 level, as pair's attempt at breaching that level had failed earlier this month, due to hefty exporter selling there, says local bank trader. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2335 GMT [Dow Jones] HK short-selling volume +37.0% at HK$3.446 billion yesterday, as percentage of market total tad higher at 6.2% vs Monday's 5.4%, suggesting bears eyeing more near-term market downside amid HSI's 3-day losing streak. China Mobile (0941.HK) topped list with HK$458.05 million, followed by \uc2 Hutchison Whampoa\uc2  (0013.HK) with HK$173.62 million, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  (0005.HK) with HK$162.87 million. Chalco (2600.HK), \uc2 Li & Fung\uc2  (0494.HK) rounded out top 5, with HK$150.29 million, HK$135.23 million respectively. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2327 GMT [Dow Jones] Gold boun